{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"9db9deb60148098d2558053f0af4063bb80616d3a93ce60a75037989b596e629","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_d0b016ecdb33ee2d07bacf376904fc3a50a3a53037f956bb837bddb614b35d2e","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a novel optimization algorithm with strong theoretical grounding. However, it fails to adhere to double-blind review policies by revealing author identities and affiliations. Additionally, it lacks a dedicated section on ethics, broader impact, and societal considerations, which are standard expectations for contemporary machine learning research. Data usage is compliant with standard practices for public datasets.","paper_id":"B1YfAfcgl","paper_identity_sha256":"4cb99404359c679d8b35f3175dd9adaad545c192bd46238e885332e2daaa2e7b","prompt_identity_sha256":"28172f24d3e61024a6ade4e9559c6069e400ab98c6718aa72e09bbbb63257a99","raw_response_sha256":"a6f8d24871c67d7cc47517e075fdc0d05051adf8b785bbd60b49efee21edbf92","request_identity_sha256":"aeaebbc3a580c5625310999f01d212ff94f13ce0dbc7d467d404b36b5eef8ac7","reviewer_identity_sha256":"6832030d37bc6b05f4de12f913ecdea182594ad5d7ac3dcd33edcb54d7bd3a1a","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v2","structural_context_sha256":"ec8cc86da9d81ce8a38b5be410cca5062f602d489d08646f9fd3ed8657b0909d","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a dedicated section on ethics, fairness, or responsible AI. As an optimization algorithm for standard image classification tasks (MNIST, CIFAR-10), the immediate ethical risks are low, but the lack of discussion on potential biases in the datasets or the broader societal impact of the optimization technique is a minor omission. The authors do not discuss fairness or harms to marginalized populations, which is typical for theoretical optimization papers of this era but represents a gap in comprehensive ethical consideration.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-006","SRC-029"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes standard public datasets: MNIST (LeCun et al., 1998) and CIFAR-10 (Krizhevsky, 2009). These datasets are widely used in machine learning research and are generally considered to be in the public domain or available under permissive licenses for research purposes. The paper does not mention any personally identifiable information (PII) or sensitive data, as the datasets consist of handwritten digits and natural images of objects. There is no indication of privacy violations or misuse of licensed data. The use of these datasets appears compliant with standard research practices.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (Pratik Chaudhari, Anna Choromanska, Stefano Soatto, Yann LeCun) and their institutional affiliations (UCLA, NYU, Facebook AI Research) on the first page. It also provides direct email addresses for all authors. This violates the double-blind review policy typically enforced at venues like ICLR, as it allows reviewers to identify the authors and their affiliations. The presence of these details compromises the anonymity required for fair peer review.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-007","SRC-008"],"review_text":"The paper cites relevant prior work extensively, including studies on the energy landscape of deep networks (Choromanska et al., 2015a;b; Chaudhari & Soatto, 2015) and related optimization techniques. There is no evidence of plagiarism or self-plagiarism in the visible text. The content appears to be original, building upon cited theoretical foundations without uncredited reuse of material. No dual submission issues are apparent from the text provided.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-040"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a specific 'Broader Impact' statement or a checklist for societal considerations, which are increasingly required in modern ML conferences. While the work is primarily theoretical and algorithmic, the absence of a discussion on the broader implications of the optimization method (e.g., computational costs, environmental impact of training, or potential misuse) is a limitation. The acknowledgements section mentions funding from ONR, AFOSR, and ARO, but there is no mention of IRB approval or ethics review, which is not strictly necessary for this type of work but is part of a complete compliance profile. The lack of explicit licensing information for any released code or data is also a minor gap, though not critical for a theoretical paper.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"83cd5d20d62812baea95cc6f6fbdfe988d7dcf9e8525f6f4beae714c47cfadec","paper_id":"B1YfAfcgl","paper_ordinal":12,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"a6f8d24871c67d7cc47517e075fdc0d05051adf8b785bbd60b49efee21edbf92","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"B1YfAfcgl","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"50b6d5f288706883ea5484311734daeef067159404f1d270182112da16c6e7d2","request_identity_sha256":"aeaebbc3a580c5625310999f01d212ff94f13ce0dbc7d467d404b36b5eef8ac7","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v2","usage":{"completion_tokens":918,"prompt_tokens":18136,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":19054},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"aeaebbc3a580c5625310999f01d212ff94f13ce0dbc7d467d404b36b5eef8ac7","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v1"}